Section 1 (Section 16-23-210(h)): "Assault weapon" means a firearm with any of the following characteristics: (i) all semiautomatic action, centerfire rifles with a detachable magazine with a capacity of twenty-one or more rounds; (ii) all semiautomatic shotguns with a folding stock or a magazine capacity of more than six rounds, or both;
Section 2 (new Section 16-23-290): No person in this State may manufacture, import, distribute, sell, or offer for sale any assault weapon, except as authorized in this section.
Section 2 (new Section 16-23-290): A person who violates this section is guilty of a misdemeanor and, upon conviction, must be imprisoned not more than three years.
